---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Dynamic (not prerendered) because BaseLayout's nav/footer depend on
// live per-request session and locale state via Astro.cookies.
export const prerender = false;

// Written from how the site actually handles data; not yet reviewed by a
// lawyer. Have it reviewed before relying on it for compliance (e.g. GDPR
// for EU visitors). This used to be a public banner, removed 26 Sep 2026
// because payment-network reviewers read it as an incomplete policy.
// Apple sign-in is built but not switched on, so only Google is named
// below (same in terms.astro); add Apple back when it is.
const lastUpdated = '30 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — IWIS Global" description="How IWIS Global collects, uses, and protects your information when you book a tour or create an account.">
  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-serif font-semibold mb-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 mb-6">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      IWIS Global ("we", "us") operates this website to sell private Agra and Taj Mahal tours. This policy
      explains what information we collect when you use it, and how it's used.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Information we collect</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-stone-700 space-y-1 mb-6">
      <li><strong>Booking details:</strong> when you book a tour, we collect your name, email address, and phone number, along with your chosen tour, travel date, and traveler count.</li>
      <li><strong>Payment:</strong> payments are processed by Razorpay. We never see or store your card, UPI, or bank details — Razorpay handles that directly, and we only receive confirmation that a payment succeeded.</li>
      <li><strong>Account information (optional):</strong> if you sign in with Google, we receive your name, email address, and profile photo from Google, so you can view your booking history. If you create an account with an email and password instead, we store your email address and a one-way hash of your password — never the password itself. To block password guessing, we also record the IP address and number of failed attempts when someone signs in with an email and password.</li>
      <li><strong>Entry tickets:</strong> for tours that include monument entry tickets (or when you add them), we buy the tickets on the Archaeological Survey of India's (ASI) official website using the traveler names and nationalities its ticketing requires. We keep a copy of the e-ticket file with your booking and email it to you.</li>
      <li><strong>Questions to our AI guide:</strong> questions you type into the "YourGuide" box on our homepage are sent to Anthropic's Claude AI to write the answer. We don't store your questions; to limit how often the box can be used, we keep a one-way hash of your IP address (not the address itself) and the time of each question.</li>
      <li><strong>Reviews:</strong> after your tour we may email or WhatsApp you a private link to rate it. If you leave a review, we store your rating and comments with your booking. Once we've checked it, we publish it on our website with your first name and last initial, the tour, and the month you traveled. You can edit your review through the same link, or ask us to remove it.</li>
      <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> your chosen language and currency are stored in cookies on your device so the site remembers them on your next visit.</li>
      <li><strong>Enquiries by WhatsApp, phone or email:</strong> if you contact us before booking, we may record your name, contact details, message and the tour you're interested in, so we can follow up. The messages themselves also travel through WhatsApp (Meta) or your email provider, under their own privacy practices.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics (cookies only if you accept):</strong> this site uses Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site — for example, which pages are visited and general navigation patterns. If you tap Accept on our cookie banner, it collects standard usage data (pages viewed, approximate location, device/browser type) using analytics cookies. If you tap Reject, or haven't chosen yet, Google Analytics sets no cookies; Google may still receive basic signals without cookies or an identifier, such as that a page was viewed. When you book, we also send Google Analytics the tour, amount, currency, number of travelers and payment reference — linked to your browser's analytics ID only if you accepted cookies, and never with your name or contact details. It is not used to identify you personally.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising (only if you accept):</strong> if you tap Accept on our cookie banner, the Meta Pixel records which pages you visit and, when you book, the tour, amount paid, currency and payment reference, so we can show our tours to you on Instagram and Facebook and measure which ads lead to bookings. We never send Meta your name, email or phone number. If you tap Reject, the Meta Pixel doesn't load.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">How we use this information</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-stone-700 space-y-1 mb-2">
      <li>To process and confirm your booking, buy any entry tickets it includes, and contact you about it.</li>
      <li>To let you sign in and view your booking history, if you create an account.</li>
      <li>To respond to questions you send us, and follow up on enquiries.</li>
      <li>To ask for a review after your tour, and publish the reviews guests choose to leave.</li>
      <li>To meet legal and accounting obligations (e.g. retaining payment records).</li>
      <li>To understand overall site usage via Google Analytics, so we can improve the site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">We do not sell your personal information.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Who we share it with</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-stone-700 space-y-1 mb-2">
      <li><strong>Razorpay</strong> — to process payments.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> — only if you choose to sign in with it.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — our hosting and database provider; your requests pass through their infrastructure to reach our servers.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> — via Google Analytics, for the site-usage and booking analytics described above.</li>
      <li><strong>Meta (Facebook, Instagram)</strong> — via the Meta Pixel, only if you accept advertising cookies, for the advertising described above.</li>
      <li><strong>Resend</strong> — the email service that sends your booking confirmation, e-tickets and review requests (it receives your name, email address, and booking details).</li>
      <li><strong>Archaeological Survey of India (ASI)</strong> — traveler names and nationalities, only when we buy monument entry tickets for your tour.</li>
      <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> — the text of questions you type into the YourGuide box, to generate the answer.</li>
      <li><strong>Open-Meteo and Google</strong> — some pages load content directly from them in your browser (the Agra weather card from Open-Meteo; the "Add to Preferred Sources" button on our blog from Google), which means they see your IP address like any website you visit.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">We don't share your information with anyone else for marketing purposes.</p>

    <h2 id="cookies" class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 scroll-mt-24">Cookies</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-2">This site uses a small number of cookies. Most make the site work. The Google Analytics cookies, which measure site usage, and the Meta advertising cookies are set only if you tap Accept on our cookie banner:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-stone-700 space-y-1 mb-6">
      <li><code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">currency</code> and <code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">lang</code> — remember your preferred currency and language.</li>
      <li><code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">customer_session</code> — keeps you signed in, if you have an account.</li>
      <li><code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">admin_session</code> — staff-only, used to access the booking management system.</li>
      <li><code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">oauth_state</code> — a short-lived cookie used only during Google sign-in, deleted immediately after.</li>
      <li><code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">_ga</code>, <code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">_ga_*</code> — set by Google Analytics, only if you accept, to distinguish visitors and measure site usage.</li>
      <li><code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">cookie_consent</code> — remembers whether you accepted or rejected analytics and advertising cookies, for 180 days.</li>
      <li><code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">_fbp</code>, <code class="text-sm bg-stone-100 px-1 rounded">_fbc</code> — set by the Meta Pixel, only if you accept, to recognise your browser for Instagram and Facebook ads.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">You can change your choice at any time with “Cookie settings” at the bottom of every page. Rejecting removes the Google Analytics and Meta cookies from this site.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Data retention</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">We keep booking records for as long as needed for accounting, legal, and customer-support purposes. You can ask us to delete your account and associated personal data by contacting us — see below.</p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Your choices</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">
      You can book a tour as a guest without creating an account. If you do sign in, you can stop using that
      account at any time, and can ask us to delete your data by contacting us. You can accept or reject
      analytics and advertising cookies, and change that choice later, with “Cookie settings” at the bottom of every page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">Contact us</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700">
      Questions about this policy or your data can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:info@iwisglobal.com" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">info@iwisglobal.com</a> or via
      <a href={`https://wa.me/916399226633?text=${encodeURIComponent('Hi! (ref: PRIVACY)')}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-wa-ref="PRIVACY" class="text-brand-800 hover:underline">WhatsApp</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
